WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.510
The Odyssey is one of the oldest stories ever told, nearly 3,000 years old. But the entire 10-year nightmare happened because one man couldn't keep his mouth

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:14.150
shut after winning a fight. Yeah, seriously. Odysseus had already escaped.

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:23.110
He was safely sailing away when he turned around and shouted his real name at the monster he'd just blinded. That single moment of ego turned what should

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:32.310
have been a 2-week voyage into 10 years of monsters, shipwrecks, angry gods, and disaster. He left Troy with 12 ships and

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:41.630
more than 600 men. Not one of them made it home. A witch turned his crew into pigs, a six-headed monster devoured his sailors, and even the gods themselves

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:51.110
wanted him dead. So, how did the smartest man in ancient Greece outsmart himself for an entire decade? Let's start at the end of the Trojan War. For

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:59.350
10 years, the Greeks had camped outside the walls of Troy, right here on the coast of modern-day Turkey. The Trojans wouldn't come out, and the Greeks

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:09.430
couldn't get in. Odysseus had an idea. Build a giant wooden horse, hide soldiers inside, and leave it at the gates as a gift. Are we sure this is going to work? Trust me. Everyone loves

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:17.950
a gift horse. What if they look inside? Who looks inside a horse? The Trojans dragged it through the gates. That night, the Greeks climbed out, opened

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:23.030
the gates, and burned Troy to the ground. War over, Odysseus was a hero.

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:29.190
Now all he had to do was sail home to his wife Penelope and his son Telemachus on the island of Ithaca, right here.

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:37.510
Should have taken about 2 weeks. It took 10 years. The first stop was Ismarus, right here, home of Cicones. Odysseus

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:46.790
and his men raided the city, grabbed treasure and wine, and Odysseus told his men to get back on the ships. Did they listen? Of course not. They stayed on

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:56.590
the beach and partied all night. The next morning, the Cicones came back with reinforcements and killed 72 of Odysseus's men, six from each of his 12

00:01:56.600 --> 00:02:06.469
ships. Day one of the trip home and he's already burying soldiers. After that, a storm blew them off course for nine days. Banded up at the island of Lotus

00:02:06.479 --> 00:02:16.470
Eaters. Anyone who ate the lotus forgot everything. Their home, their family, their entire life. Just gone. Three of Odysseus' scouts ate it and had to be

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:26.430
dragged back to the ships crying. Not the worst stop on the trip. That honor goes to the next one. So, how did one cave on one island turn into the biggest

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:36.910
mistake of Odysseus' life? They landed on the island of Cyclopes. Odysseus took 12 of his best men and explored a cave filled with cheese and lambs. His men

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:46.150
wanted to grab the food and leave. Odysseus said no. He wanted to meet the owner. The owner turned out to be Polyphemus, a one-eyed giant and son of

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:55.390
Poseidon, the god of the sea. Polyphemus rolled a boulder over the cave entrance that was so heavy that 22 wagons couldn't move it. They were trapped. The

00:02:55.400 --> 00:03:05.310
Cyclops grabbed two of Odysseus' men, smashed their heads on the ground, and ate them raw. He did the same thing the next morning. Two more men for breakfast. Odysseus couldn't kill the

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:15.030
Cyclops because then nobody could move the boulder. So, he offered the giant wine. Lots of it. Cyclops, what's your name? Polyphemus. What's yours? My name

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:20.830
is Nobody. Nobody? Well, Nobody, I like you. I'll eat you last. That's my gift.

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:30.430
Thanks. Very generous. After the Cyclops passed out drunk, Odysseus sharpened a massive olive stake, heated it in the fire, and drove it straight into the

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:35.509
giant's eye. Polyphemus screamed for help. The other Cyclopes came running.

00:03:35.519 --> 00:03:44.150
Polyphemus, what's wrong? Who's hurting you? Nobody, he said. Nobody is hurting me. Well, nobody's hurting you. Go back to sleep. Brilliant, right? And in the

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:52.790
morning, blind Polyphemus rolled back the boulders to let his sheep out and felt each one's back to make sure no men were riding them. Odysseus and his

00:03:52.800 --> 00:04:02.390
surviving men strapped themselves to the bellies of the sheep and escaped right under the Cyclops' hands. If Odysseus had just sailed away, that would have

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:11.510
been the end of it. Poseidon would never have known. But Odysseus was too proud for that. As his ship pulled away, he stood up and shouted back at the blinded

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:19.590
giant, "Cyclops, if anyone asks who blinded you, tell them it was Odysseus, son of Laertes, king of Ithaca." His men

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:28.950
begged him to stop. He didn't care. He wanted credit, and now Polyphemus had a name. He prayed to his father, Poseidon, god of the sea, to curse Odysseus.

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:38.870
"Father Poseidon, make sure Odysseus never gets home. And if he does, let him arrive late, broken, alone, and to a house full of trouble." Poseidon heard

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:48.750
every word, and he granted every part of that prayer. From this point on, the sea itself was Odysseus' enemy. The next stop was the island of Aeolus, king of

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:58.390
the winds. Aeolus actually liked Odysseus. He put all the dangerous winds inside a leather bag and gave Odysseus a gentle west wind to carry him straight

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:07.990
home. For 9 days, they sailed perfectly. On the 10th day, Ithaca appeared on the horizon. Odysseus could see the smoke rising from the chimneys of his own

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:17.830
island. And then, he fell asleep. His crew had been staring at that bag for 9 days, wondering what treasure was inside. The moment Odysseus closed his

00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:23.150
eyes, they opened it. &gt;&gt; What do you think is in there? &gt;&gt; Probably gold. He's been guarding it the whole trip.

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:33.590
&gt;&gt; Let's just take a peek. Every trapped wind exploded out at once and blew all 12 ships all the way back across the sea. Within sight of home and now

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:39.510
further away than ever, Odysseus begged Aeolus for help again. Aeolus refused.

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:44.110
"The gods clearly hate you. Get off my island." But the worst was still coming.

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:54.190
The Laestrygonians were giants, all of them. And when the fleet sailed into their harbor, they attacked from the cliffs. They hurled boulders down onto the ships and speared the crews like

00:05:54.200 --> 00:06:02.950
fish. 11 of 12 ships destroyed. Hundreds of men killed. Only Odysseus's ship escaped because he'd parked outside the

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:13.430
harbor. 12 ships became one. Over 500 men became a few dozen. And they hadn't even reached the halfway point. They washed up on the island of Aeaea, home

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:23.350
of the witch goddess Circe. Odysseus sent a scouting party led by his officer Eurylochus. Circe invited them in for a feast. They ate. She touched them with

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:32.790
her wand and every single one of them turned into pigs. Eurylochus hadn't gone inside. He ran back to the ship in a panic. "She turned them into pigs!" "All

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:38.950
of them?" "Every single one! They've got snouts and hooves and everything!" Odysseus went to rescue his men alone.

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:48.390
The god Hermes gave him a plant called moly that blocked Circe's magic. When her spell failed, she turned the men back and invited everyone to stay. They

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:57.870
stayed for a year on the magical island while Penelope waited at home wondering if her husband was dead. Eventually, his men had to remind him. "Sir, are we ever

00:06:57.880 --> 00:07:07.430
going home?" "Right! Home! Yes. Let's do that." Circe told him he couldn't go home yet. First, he had to sail to the land of the dead and speak with the

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:14.830
prophet Tiresias. So, Odysseus sailed to the edge of the world, dug a pit, filled it with blood, and summoned the dead.

00:07:14.840 --> 00:07:24.270
Tiresias gave him one warning. "Do not touch the cattle of the sun god Helios or you will lose everything." While he was down there, Odysseus saw his own

00:07:24.280 --> 00:07:32.510
mother. She had died of grief waiting for him to come home. He tried to embrace her three times. She slipped through his arms like a shadow. That's

00:07:32.520 --> 00:07:42.470
what his ego had cost him. Odysseus now headed into the most dangerous stretch of water in the ancient world. First, the Sirens. Beautiful voices that lured

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:51.390
sailors to crash on the rocks. Odysseus ordered his crew to plug their ears with beeswax and tie him to the mast so he could hear the song without steering

00:07:51.400 --> 00:08:02.550
toward it. "Tie me tighter." "Sir, you told us not to untie you no matter what." "I changed my mind. Untie me now." "Uh you also told us to ignore that." Next came Scylla and Charybdis.

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:12.590
Scylla was a six-headed monster on one side. Charybdis was a massive whirlpool on the other. No safe path. Odysseus chose Scylla, knowing he would lose six

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:21.670
men instead of the entire ship. Scylla snatched six sailors and ate them alive while they screamed his name. Now came the island Tiresias had warned him

00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:31.750
about, Thrinacia, home of the sacred cattle of Helios. Odysseus told his men not to touch them, but bad winds trapped them for a month and the food ran out.

00:08:31.760 --> 00:08:39.990
While Odysseus slept, his crew slaughtered the cattle. "The gods can punish us later. We're starving now." "Odysseus said not to touch them."

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:48.070
"Odysseus is asleep and I'd rather die by the sea than starve on this beach." When Odysseus woke up and smelled roasting beef, he knew they were

00:08:48.080 --> 00:08:58.150
finished. The hides of the dead cattle crawled on the ground. The meat on the spits mooed. Yeah, the meat mooed. The moment they sailed, Zeus split the ship

00:08:58.160 --> 00:09:05.590
in half with a thunderbolt. Every man drowned. Every single one. Only Odysseus survived by clinging to the wreckage.

00:09:05.600 --> 00:09:14.870
The sea washed him up on the island of Ogygia, right here, home of the goddess Calypso. She fell in love with him and offered him immortality if he would stay

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:23.630
forever. Odysseus said no. He sat on the beach every day staring at the horizon and crying for seven years. Finally,

00:09:23.640 --> 00:09:32.790
Athena convinced Zeus to intervene. He sent Hermes to tell Calypso to let Odysseus go. "Zeus says to release him." "Of course. When a goddess loves a

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:41.990
mortal, the gods always interfere." "Are Are going to let him go or not?" "Fine, but I'm not giving him a ship. Odysseus built a raft and sailed for 17 days.

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:47.070
Poseidon spotted him and smashed it into pieces because Poseidon wasn't done.

00:09:47.080 --> 00:09:57.270
Odysseus washed up on the island of Phaeacia where King Alcinous heard his story and gave him a ship home. He woke up on the beach of Ithaca 20 years after

00:09:57.280 --> 00:10:07.870
he had left. So, what had been happening at home for 20 years? A disaster. 108 men from the surrounding islands had moved into Odysseus's palace eating his

00:10:07.880 --> 00:10:12.190
food, drinking his wine, and trying to force Penelope to marry one of them.

00:10:12.200 --> 00:10:21.990
They assumed Odysseus was dead. Penelope had been holding them off with one of the greatest stalling tactics in history. She told the suitors she would choose a husband after she finished

00:10:22.000 --> 00:10:30.030
weaving a burial shroud for Odysseus's father. Every day she wove, every night she unraveled her work. Three years

00:10:30.040 --> 00:10:38.070
before a servant gave her away. The goddess Athena disguised Odysseus as an old beggar so he could enter his own home without being recognized. As he

00:10:38.080 --> 00:10:48.110
walked through the gates, an ancient dog lying on a pile of manure lifted its head. It was Argos, the hunting dog Odysseus had raised as a puppy 20 years

00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:56.310
ago. The dog wagged its tail, laid its ears flat, and died. It had waited 20 years just to see its master one last

00:10:56.320 --> 00:11:04.510
time. "Who's that old beggar?" "Ah, nobody important." "Then why is that dying dog wagging his tail at him?" Inside the palace, the suitors mocked

00:11:04.520 --> 00:11:13.070
him, threw food at him, and treated him like garbage. One of them threw a stool at his head. Odysseus took it all watching, counting, and planning.

00:11:13.080 --> 00:11:22.790
Penelope announced a contest. Whoever could string Odysseus's great bow and shoot an arrow through 12 ax heads in a row would win her hand. One by one, the

00:11:22.800 --> 00:11:27.750
suitors tried. Not a single one could even bend the bow, let alone string it.

00:11:27.760 --> 00:11:37.430
The old beggar asked for a turn. The suitors laughed. Odysseus took the bow, strung it like it was nothing, and fired an arrow clean through all 12 axes. And

00:11:37.440 --> 00:11:46.430
then, he turned the bow on the suiters. "You thought your king was dead? You devoured his home, you harassed his wife, you plotted to kill his son, and

00:11:46.440 --> 00:11:54.750
now pay for all of it." He and Telemachus killed all 108 suiters in the great hall. It was a bloodbath, but

00:11:54.760 --> 00:12:02.870
Penelope still wasn't convinced. 20 years is a long time. She had one final test. "Servants, move the king's bed out

00:12:02.880 --> 00:12:11.750
of the bedroom for our guest." "Move the bed? That bed can't be moved. I built it myself around a living olive tree. One of the bed posts is the tree itself,

00:12:11.760 --> 00:12:19.950
still rooted in the ground. Nobody knows that except me and you." That was the answer only the real Odysseus could give. Penelope broke down. They were

00:12:19.960 --> 00:12:28.510
finally reunited. 20 years, two wars, a curse from a god, six-headed monsters, witches, and a decade of suiters, and it

00:12:28.520 --> 00:12:38.110
all ended with a man remembering how he built his own bed. The Odyssey is nearly 3,000 years old, and the whole thing comes down to the same lesson it's been

00:12:38.120 --> 00:12:47.990
teaching since the 8th century BC. The smartest person in the room can still be the dumbest person in the room if they can't control their ego. Odysseus

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:56.990
outsmarted Cyclops, resisted the sirens, and navigated the land of the dead, but it took him 10 years to learn the one thing he should have known all along.

00:12:57.000 --> 00:13:05.950
Sometimes, the smartest move is keeping your mouth shut. If you'd rather listen than watch, whether you're cooking, driving, working, gaming, or falling

00:13:05.960 --> 00:13:10.400
asleep, we're on Spotify, too. Links in the description.
